    {
      "id": "food-recipe-pantry",
      "vertical": "food",
      "kind": "card",
      "request": "What can I make for dinner with eggs, tomatoes and leftover rice?",
      "says": "Fried rice, and the day-old rice is exactly what it wants.",
      "surface": "page",
      "fresh": false,
      "components": [
        "Recipe"
      ],
      "rationale": "Built from what they have: time and servings as numbers, then ingredients and numbered steps; the pantry basics it assumes are in Details.",
      "document": {
        "kind": "output_blocks",
        "major": 1,
        "header": {
          "title": "Tomato egg fried rice",
          "subtitle": "Serves 2 · one pan"
        },
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "numbers",
            "items": [
              {
                "value": "20 min",
                "label": "Total time"
              },
              {
                "value": "2",
                "label": "Serves"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "sections": [
              {
                "heading": "Ingredients",
                "bullets": [
                  "3 eggs, beaten with a pinch of salt",
                  "2 ripe tomatoes, cut in wedges",
                  "2 cups cooked rice, a day old if you have it",
                  "2 spring onions, sliced, if you have them",
                  "1 tbsp light soy sauce, 1 tbsp oil"
                ]
              },
              {
                "heading": "Method",
                "paragraphs": [
                  "1. Scramble the eggs in the hot oil until just set, then tip them out.",
                  "2. Fry the tomatoes for 3 minutes until they soften and give up their juice.",
                  "3. Add the rice and soy sauce, press out any lumps and fry for 4 minutes.",
                  "4. Fold the eggs back in and finish with the spring onions."
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "details": {
          "assumptions": [
            "Uses what you listed plus oil, salt and soy sauce; the spring onions are optional."
          ]
        },
        "fallback_text": "Tomato egg fried rice for 2, about 20 min, one pan. You need 3 eggs beaten with a pinch of salt, 2 tomatoes, 2 cups cooked rice, 2 spring onions if you have them, 1 tbsp light soy sauce and 1 tbsp oil. 1. Scramble the eggs until just set, tip out. 2. Fry the tomatoes 3 min. 3. Add the rice and soy, fry 4 min. 4. Fold the eggs back in, finish with spring onions."
      },
